>> title: Gigantes Plaki
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, tomato, greek, oven, vegetarian
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: gigantes, gigandes plaki, giant baked beans, Greek baked beans
>> pairs-with: tzatziki, pita-bread
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 45 min
>> slack: narrow — the beans come out of the first pot barely tender and no further, because they have an hour in the oven still to do and a bean that was soft before it went in comes out as skins in sauce; the hour uncovered is where the top browns and it is the one part worth watching
>> step.2: simmer 1 hr, drain
>> step.3: sweat 10 min
>> step.4: simmer 10 min
>> step.5: fold in
>> step.6: bake 350°F (180°C) 1 hr, top

Preheat the #oven{} to 350°F (180°C).

Simmer @dried gigante beans{1%lb}(450 g; soaked overnight) in @water{10%cups}(2.4 L) until barely tender, ~{1%hr}, then drain.

Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(chopped), @carrot{1}(diced), and @garlic{4%cloves} in @extra-virgin olive oil{1/2%cup}(120 mL) in a #skillet{} for ~{10%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)vegetables{} for ~{10%min} with @canned crushed tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g), @tomato paste{2%Tbs}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, and @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

Fold @&(~3)beans{} into @&(~1)sauce{} and pour into a #baking dish{}.

Bake @&(~1)beans{} uncovered at 350°F until the top browns and the sauce sets, ~{1%hr}, then scatter @crumbled feta{4%oz}(115 g) and @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup} over.
